   CONFERENCE (IRSEC' 16)},
Series = {International Renewable and Sustainable Energy Conference IRSEC},
Year = {2016},
Pages = {1050-1055},
Note = {4th International Renewable and Sustainable Energy Conference (IRSEC),
   Marrakech, MOROCCO, NOV 14-17, 2016},
Abstract = {To avoid load peaks periods and reduce the electricity bill price, it is
   necessary to jeopardize appliances models and requirements. That allows
   controlling equipment energy needs and customizing the global home
   consumption profile. This paper gives smart home appliances modeling
   aiming to generate their energy power profiles according to local
   environmental circumstances. Moreover, the proposed models take into
   account the users preferences and decisions. Therefore, the home energy
   efficiency can be enhanced. Appliances models are developed and
   simulated in Matlab/Simulink environment. Simulation results showed both
   environmental and customer behavior impact on energy consumption. Real
   case study parameters of Rabat city are used in this work.},
