   of Brescia},
Booktitle = {2018 AEIT INTERNATIONAL ANNUAL CONFERENCE},
Year = {2018},
Note = {110th AEIT International Annual Conference, Bari, ITALY, OCT 03-05, 2018},
Organization = {AEIT Sezione Pugliese; IEEE; IES},
Abstract = {The progressive paradigm shift from the centralized generation of
   electricity towards decarbonized and distributed energy systems is
   deeply changing the way energy is produced, distributed, and consumed. A
   relevant attention is currently being paid to the development of
   innovative control strategies for the management of the increasing
   complexity of power demand and generation patterns. Several research
   studies investigated this topic, by making use of simulation and
   emulation environments. However, this model-based approach may present
   relevant limitations when applied in real operating environments, due to
   the stochastic nature of real-world use cases. The aim of this study is
   thus to present a testing infrastructure able to deploy and test
   innovative Smart Grid and energy concepts in a real environment, by
   making use of operating energy assets and of real users' behavior and
   power demand profiles.},
