Abstract = {Thermal comfort conditions in the built environment are strictly related
   not only to the thermal and geometric building features and to
   air-conditioning systems, but also to the building using profile and to
   the biological-metabolic-psychologicaI characteristics of the users.
   Consequently it is useful to formalize new models, both subjective and
   adaptive to the environmental scenery, in a particular holistic vision
   of the problem, strongly addressed towards the personalization of the
   service.
   Through the paper the characterization of a model, enriching that
   proposed by Fanger with an adaptive approach, is carried out using a
   Multi Agent System (AIMS), an Intelligent Agent able to follow user in
   his own needs and preferences and to adapt to the changes of context
   variables.},
